BEGIN_PGML
Build a spreadsheet that computes the difference between [`f(x)`] and [`L(x)`] for [`x`]-values between [`-1`] and [`1\text{,}`] spaced [`0.1`] units apart. *Note:* we will revisit this spreadsheet for additional computations in Activity[$NBSP]*8.1.12, so it would be ideal if you save your work electronically in place you can find it later.

Your spreadsheet should start like the following table:

>> [@DataTable(
  [
    [
     [PGML('Row'),
      rowbottom => '1',
      midrule => '1',],
     PGML('[`\Delta x`]'),
     PGML('[`x`]'),
     PGML('[`f(x) = e^x`]'),
     PGML('[`L(x) = 1 + x`]'),
    ],
    [
     [PGML('0'),
      rowbottom => '1',
      midrule => '1',],
     PGML('[`0.1`]'),
     PGML('[`-1.0`]'),
     PGML('[`0.36787\ldots`]'),
     PGML('[`0.0`]'),
    ],
    [
     [PGML('1'),
      rowbottom => '1',
      midrule => '1',],
     PGML('[`0.1`]'),
     PGML('[`-0.9`]'),
     PGML('[`0.40656\ldots`]'),
     PGML('[`0.1`]'),
    ],
    [
     [PGML('2'),
      rowbottom => '1',
      midrule => '1',],
     PGML('[`0.1`]'),
     PGML('[`-0.8`]'),
     PGML('[`0.44932\ldots`]'),
     PGML('[`0.2`]'),
    ],
    [
     [PGML('⋮'),
      rowbottom => '1',
      midrule => '1',],
     PGML('⋮'),
     PGML('⋮'),
     PGML('⋮'),
     PGML('⋮'),
    ],
  ],
      align => '!{\vrule width 0.11em}c|c|c|c|c!{\vrule width 0.11em}',
      valign => 'middle',
      top => '3',);@]* <<

Then Row 14 is:

>> [@DataTable(
  [
    [
     [PGML('Row'),
      rowbottom => '1',
      midrule => '1',],
     PGML('[`\Delta x`]'),
     PGML('[`x`]'),
     PGML('[`f(x) = e^x`]'),
     PGML('[`L(x) = 1 + x`]'),
    ],
    [
     [PGML('14'),
      rowbottom => '1',
      midrule => '1',],
     PGML('[_]{0.1}{3}'),
     PGML('[_]{0.4}{3}'),
     PGML('[_]{exp(0.4)}{3}'),
     PGML('[_]{1.4}{3}'),
    ],
  ],
      align => '!{\vrule width 0.11em}c|c|c|c|c!{\vrule width 0.11em}',
      valign => 'middle',
      top => '3',);@]* <<

